[#:seon.task{:name "the-branch-evidence-gate-rarely-sees-red-before-on-main"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Default's main holds no recorded result for any of the 30 tests reaching seon.cluster.branch/cluster-branch (2026-10-08): tests run in throwaway JVMs, not on main. A test red before a lane's change therefore reads as unproven, not red-before, unless root runs it on main first. Done when main carries current results for the tests the gate asks about (root's merge or a scheduled run), or the gate takes red-before evidence from an unchanged fork of the head."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.branch-evidence/branch-evidence seon.test/recorded-result}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-agent-check-costs-ten-times-its-one-test"
             :kind :function
             :intent "my.test/check {:seon.test/changed [seon.agent/archived?]} on a lane branch took 6.4 s and 8.9 s for one test whose run was 0.53 s (acquire 95 ms), about 110,000 calls, seon.schema/projection-cache-value about 19,000 times (2026-10-08). A defn and its check in one eval request recorded evidence for the pre-defn digest, so the branch-evidence gate correctly refused it as unproven until a second check. Done when one reaching test's check is under 1.5 s and evidence from a defn plus check in one request is current."
             :must-read #{my.test/check seon.test/run}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-printer-failure-answers-unprintable-without-its-cause"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A JVM eval_clj whose value was [rows kw (keys @conn)] answered `#unprintable[clojure.lang.PersistentVector java.lang.ClassCastException]` with no diagnostic naming the failing member or cause (2026-10-08, agent impl-rf2). Done when the printer shows the printable members and names the failing path, with its error delivered beside the value. More evidence (default, 2026-10-08): in the SCI path (keys [1 2]) printed a diagnostic with a 76-frame stack (~3,500 tokens, ClassCastException in KeySeq) while JVM mode shows only #unprintable[...] with no diagnostic. Done also when the diagnostic is compact data (type, message, top frames; ledger PR-04) in both modes. Owners: seon.sci.eval/shown-result and the diagnostic builder."
             :must-read #{seon.mcp/call}}
 #:seon.task{:name "agent-identity-prints-its-id-into-the-message"
             :kind :function
             :intent "seon.agent/identity builds :seon.error/message with (pr-str agent-id), a second printer; the id is already the :seon.agent/no-such-agent member. No test reaches seon.agent/identity, so the branch-evidence gate refuses its change as unreached. Done when the message is fixed text and a test reaches the function."
             :must-read #{seon.agent/identity}}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-branch-evidence-commit-is-dominated-by-whole-tree-lint"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The first --branch-evidence commit (e11bb03b9, 2026-10-08) took 10.8 s wall: the gate answered in 175 ms and clj-kondo over the whole candidate tree (src script test, --cache false) took 9.6 s for a one-line change. Done when a one-file branch-evidence commit lints only what the change can affect (the changed files, with the cached analysis of the rest) and finishes under 2 s."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.branch-evidence/branch-evidence}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-lane-branch-does-not-survive-a-default-restart"
             :kind :function
             :intent "After default restarted on e3b7bae3a (2026-10-08), agent impl-rf2-dogfood held no branch on cluster default: its defn of seon.agent/archived? and green evidence were gone, so bin/lane evidence answered unavailable (85 ms) until the defn was evaluated again (its automatic test step re-ran the reaching test green). Done when a lane agent's branch and evidence survive a restart that keeps the store, or the restart's reset of agents is stated and bin/lane names it."
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.branch-evidence/branch-evidence}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-reaching-red-is-proven-red-before-by-its-result-at-the-base-key"
             :kind :function
             :intent "(hybrid-test-results R9) `--branch-evidence` reads the same answer as the step, and the accepted list goes. `seon.cluster.branch-evidence/test-evidence` sorts reaching reds by `seon.test.runner/results-at` at the cluster head under `:interpreted` and passes the reached set once: red is `:seon.source/red-before` (proves, named in the trailer), green is `:seon.source/broken` (refuses), unknown names the form that runs its base. It runs nothing and needs no execution handle. Delete `seon.test.runner/red-at-current-reach?`, `--accept-red-before`, `bin/lane evidence ... -- TEST`, the accepted trailer, `:seon.source/accepted-red-before` and `verdict`'s `accepted`, converting the callers: `bin/lane`, `resources/seon/schemas/seon.source.edn`, `test/seon/cluster/branch_evidence_test.clj`, the must-read of `seon.turn/a-reached-test-unrun-or-red-on-main-does-not-block-done` and `seon.cluster.source/a-test-never-run-on-the-target-is-not-blamed-on-the-merge`, the intent in `resources/seon/tasks/seon.task.edn`, `docs/seon/schedule/cards/{RF-2,ROOT-AGENT}.md`, the evidence; the `seon.operator.edn` intent is R10's. Host-bound slice (`bin/`): `bin/lane commit` with `--test seon.cluster.branch-evidence-test`. Red proof: `seon.cluster.branch-evidence-test/a-branch-proves-its-files-only-with-current-green-evidence`: the red-before case asserts `:proven?` true with no accepted set, and a new `testing` shows green at H and red on the branch is in `:seon.source/broken` and refuses (HEAD: proven only when accepted). Cost: answer under 1 s over the prepl, no test run. Supersedes `seon.cluster.branch-evidence/the-branch-evidence-gate-rarely-sees-red-before-on-main`. Files: `src/seon/cluster/branch_evidence.clj`, `src/seon/test/runner.clj`, `bin/lane`, `resources/seon/schemas/seon.source.edn`, `test/seon/cluster/branch_evidence_test.clj`, `resources/seon/tasks/{seon.turn,seon.cluster.source,seon.task}.edn`"
             :must-read #{seon.cluster.branch-evidence/test-evidence seon.cluster.branch-evidence/verdict seon.test.runner/red-at-current-reach? seon.test.runner/latest-results}
             :needs #{[:seon.task/sym seon.context/a-red-with-no-base-result-is-unknown]}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-test-results.md" "docs/seon/schedule/agent-loop-ledger.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/lane-templates/repl-slice.md"}}]
